{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3neqMCKd3x4rVLns39a","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't commit January. The file has a bad row, and the project check can't catch it.\n\n**The check missed it.** `scripts/check.sh` printed \"OK\", but `check.conf` says `year=2025`, so it only looks at `data/2025-*.csv` and never opened the January file. I ran the same field-count test on `data/2026-01.csv` directly, and it failed:\n\n```\nrow 33: R2601-032,C117,399.31,wholesale\n```\n\nThat row has 4 fields instead of 5. The `date` is missing.\n\nI've put the file back in `inbox/` and the working tree is clean.\n\n**To finish this, I need two decisions from you:**\n1. **The row:** do you know R2601-032's date, or should I drop the row? I'd rather not guess a value.\n2. **The check:** switching `check.conf` to `year=2026` would stop it checking the 2025 files. A better fix is to change `check.sh` to check every `data/*.csv`. That changes what your pre-commit gate does, so I haven't made either change without your go-ahead.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":340,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":18299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":232,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-27>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:16.425Z","request_id":"gen-1794703451-93aeXsFMB37RQwFkNQOC"}
